  Withheld 8 annotation(s) that describe a cell another annotation already describes — one label per cell, as a person would put it. ELEPHANT learns CENTRES, so two overlapping labels on one nucleus teach it that nucleus has two, and every round compounds it. Measured on fitted ellipses against CTC silver truth, a pair on the SAME cell overlaps at 0.98 and a pair on two cells at 0.02, so above 0.50 catches all of the first for about 10% of the second. NOTHING IS MERGED: both spots stay in the graph and both are linked, only the label is withheld — a wrong merge destroys a cell, a wrong withhold costs one round's teaching of it.
