    train payload over 10 timepoint(s): 1600 spot(s) sent — fp=0, fn=2, tp=1598 (1598 tagged tp, 0 untagged and sent as tp by default); 206 withheld as unlabeled. fp and fn are corrections and carry false_weight (10x) on the server; tp is an ordinary positive. The 2 correction(s) here therefore weigh about 1% of the labelled signal against the 1598 plain positive(s). If detection thins out from here, that balance is the first thing to look at.
